result:
Comments, deletion, reporting and auto-hiding are in. `bun run typecheck` passes, and `bun test` passes: 8 tests, including 6 new ones in `tests/CommentController.test.ts`. I didn't start the app or try the page in a browser.

The new tests run in-process and cover:
- a guest's comment redirects to `/login` and stores nothing;
- comments are stored with their author and listed oldest first, with ISO dates;
- empty and 2001-character bodies fail with the same status and redirect as an invalid post title, and store nothing;
- the comment's author and the post's author can delete; anyone else gets 403 and the comment stays;
- a repeated report returns 204 and leaves one row;
- three different reporters hide a comment from the page while the row stays in `comments`;
- deleting a post removes its comments and their reports.

Behaviours to be aware of:
- **Deleting a post:** I don't know whether SQLite enforces foreign keys on this connection, so the cascade on the tables might not fire. `PostController.destroy` therefore deletes the comments and their reports itself before the post. Deleting a comment removes its reports the same way.
- **Whitespace:** comment bodies are trimmed before the 1–2000 check, like post titles. A comment of only spaces is rejected, and stored bodies have no leading or trailing spaces.
- **Test setup:** the new tests have to get a CSRF token first (`withCsrf`); without it every change request returns 403. The tests write to the test database (`data/guren.test.db`) and don't clear it between runs; each run uses fresh email addresses so they don't collide.

**Summary:** I added `comments` and `comment_reports` tables in `db/schema.ts`, with a unique (`comment_id`, `user_id`) index, cascading foreign keys and a migration generated by drizzle-kit in `db/migrations/20260925013736_material_nightcrawler/`. New files: the `Comment` and `CommentReport` models (the latter holds the hide threshold of 3), `CommentPolicy` (registered in `AuthorizationProvider`), `CommentValidator` (body 1–2000 characters, trimmed), `CommentResource` and `CommentController`. The controller has `store`, which redirects to the post; `destroy`, which redirects for the comment's or post's author and returns 403 otherwise; and `report`, which always returns 204 and counts a repeat once. Routes are in `routes/web.ts`: `POST /posts/:id/comments` inside the existing `auth` group, plus a new `/comments` group with `DELETE /:id` and `POST /:id/report`. `PostController.show` now adds a `comments` prop, oldest first, leaving out any comment reported by three or more users. `destroy` deletes a post's comments and reports first. `resources/js/pages/posts/Show.tsx` shows the comments with author and time, a comment box when signed in, and Delete and Report buttons. I re-ran codegen to update the files in `.guren/`, and added the tests in `tests/CommentController.test.ts`.
